{"base_rate":0.172,"brier":0.08637653333333332,"bss":0.39349136801108486,"bss_hi":0.46820868738671145,"bss_lo":0.3034843431274156,"chart":{"base":[285.0,128.2],"fp":[234.3,364.4],"lead":"62,224.2 272,223.4 482,209.8 692,180","note":{"base":"skill 0.39 — higher than 67% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +1pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 25% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 3%; promised 58% → rained 61%"},"rel":"62,452.9 108.5,402.5 427,203.9"},"country":"MA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.04290666666666665,"ess":253.8154525829614,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nador</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nador rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (78%), believe about\n<b>77%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 750 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMELILLA, 12.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.39, ranked 44 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(24&ndash;74) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>430</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>95</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>77%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nador</b> <span class=\"muted\">MA</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.39</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>24&ndash;74\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>750 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nador &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nador\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 68.62,352.88 96.34378947368421,316.86315789473684 186.94328767123287,212.46575342465755 335.26935064935066,65.27272727272731 335.26935064935066,126.72727272727272 186.94328767123287,287.26027397260276 96.34378947368421,362.8421052631579 68.62,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"319.392\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"319.392\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,370.9953488372093 68.62,357.73333333333335 96.34378947368421,305.36842105263156 186.94328767123287,222.43835616438358 335.26935064935066,103.09090909090907\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 430 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"370.9953488372093\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.62\" cy=\"357.73333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 95 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"96.34378947368421\" cy=\"305.36842105263156\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 36%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"186.94328767123287\" cy=\"222.43835616438358\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 77% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"335.26935064935066\" cy=\"103.09090909090907\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nador the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.44) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.03).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'>0.030</td><td class='num'>1.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.306</td><td class='num'>3.1%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>213</td><td class='num'>21%</td><td class='num'>0.324</td><td class='num'>5.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.437</td><td class='num'>9.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":35.16813,"lon":-2.93352,"n":750,"n_cities":134,"name":"Nador","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":430,"obs":0.030232558139534883,"sig":true},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.029999999999999995,"n":75,"obs":0.06666666666666667,"sig":false},{"hi":0.22200000000000045,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.10831578947368424,"n":95,"obs":0.21052631578947367,"sig":true},{"hi":0.58,"lo":0.22200000000000045,"mean":0.36424657534246574,"n":73,"obs":0.4383561643835616,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.58,"mean":0.7832467532467532,"n":77,"obs":0.7662337662337663,"sig":false}],"prcp_km":12.3,"provisional":false,"rank":44,"rank_hi":74.02499999999998,"rank_lo":24.0,"reliability":0.0025460542524972578,"resolution":0.05597876316400392,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"nador","station":"MELILLA","timezone":"Africa/Casablanca"}